    "visibleText": "2023 - PyCon HK - Page 2 Skip to content Menu PyCon HK Conference Highlights Schedule 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 Sponsors 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 Communities 2024 2023 2022 Booths 2024 2023 Organizers 2024 2023 2022 Volunteers 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 PyCon HK Category: 2023 Discover the Future with Our Networking Hour Partner OpenSSF – PyCon HK 2023 Posted on October 10, 2023 July 20, 2025 The OpenSSF is a cross-industry organization that brings together the industry’s most important open source security initiatives and the individuals and companies that support them. The OpenSSF is committed to collaboration and working both upstream and with existing communities to advance open source security for all. Read More Discover the Future with Our Valued Prize Sponsor JetBrains – PyCon HK 2023 Posted on October 10, 2023 July 20, 2025 JetBrains is the creator of IntelliJ IDEA, ReSharper, GoLand, PyCharm, WebStorm, PhpStorm and Kotlin. We create industry leading software development tools. For over 20 years we have strived to make the strongest, most effective developer tools on Earth. By automating routine checks and corrections, our products speed up production, freeing developers to grow, discover and… Read More Discover the Future with Our Valued Bronze Sponsor Microsoft – PyCon HK 2023 Posted on October 10, 2023 July 20, 2025 Read More Discover the Future with Our Valued Silver Sponsor PCCW-HKT – PyCon HK 2023 Posted on October 10, 2023 July 20, 2025 PCCW PCCW Limited (SEHK: 0008) is a global company headquartered in Hong Kong which holds interests in telecommunications, media, IT solutions, property development and investment, and other businesses. The Company holds a majority stake in the HKT Trust and HKT Limited*, Hong Kong’s premier telecommunications service provider and leading operator of fixed-line, broadband, mobile communication… Read More Discover the Future with Our Valued Silver Sponsor MySQL – PyCon HK 2023 Posted on October 10, 2023 July 20, 2025 MySQL is the World’s Most Popular Open Source Database. It powers the most innovative companies including Facebook, Booking, Uber, and Tesla. It is available on-premises and as the MySQL Database Service on Oracle Cloud. For developers, it’s an easy to use, reliable and high-performance database with NoSQL and SQL support. SaaS, ecommerce, financial, telecom, and… Read More Discover the Future with Our Valued Gold Sponsor PSF – PyCon HK 2023 Posted on October 10, 2023 July 20, 2025 The Python Software Foundation is the organization behind Python. Become a member of the PSF and help advance the software and our mission. Read More Discover the Future with Our Valued Gold Sponsor AWS – PyCon HK 2023 Posted on October 10, 2023 July 20, 2025 About Amazon Web Services Since 2006, Amazon Web Services has been the world’s most comprehensive and broadly adopted cloud. AWS has been continually expanding its services to support virtually any workload, and it now has more than 240 fully featured services for compute, storage, databases, networking, analytics, machine learning and artificial intelligence (AI), Internet of… Read More Discover the Future with Our Valued Platinum Sponsor Red Hat – PyCon HK 2023 Posted on October 10, 2023 July 20, 2025 Red Hat is the world’s leading provider of enterprise open source solutions—including Linux, cloud, container, and Kubernetes. Red Hat delivers hardened solutions that make it easier for enterprises to work across platforms and environments, from the core datacenter to the network edge. Read More Sponsors – PyCon HK 2023 Posted on October 10, 2023 July 20, 2025 PyCon Hong Kong 2023 extends our heartfelt gratitude to our sponsors for their unwavering support. Their contributions are invaluable in spreading Python and championing the open-source cause. Please click on sponsor logos for further sponsor messages: Platinum Sponsor Gold Sponsor Silver Sponsor Bronze Sponsor Prize Sponsor Networking Hour Partner Read More Booths – PyCon HK 2023 Posted on October 10, 2023 July 27, 2025 Booths at PyCon HK 2023 are organized by the following sponsors and supporting organization. Visit them for networking and knowledge sharing. Read More Supporting Organizations – PyCon HK 2023 Posted on October 10, 2023 July 27, 2025 Special thanks to our esteemed counterparts for helping us spread the word and actively participating in PyCon Hong Kong 2023: 852Dev Cyberport AWS User Group HK Girls in Tech – Macau Google Developer Group Cloud HK HKACE Hong Kong Machine Learning Meetup HKU AI Society Hour of Code Hong Kong IVE Japanese Raspberry Pi Users… Read More Volunteers – PyCon HK 2023 Posted on October 10, 2023 November 12, 2023 Volunteers for PyCon Hong Kong 2023 are the essential builders of this conference. We deeply appreciate their countless months of hard work, making all of this possible. Read More Organizers – PyCon HK 2023 Posted on October 10, 2023 July 20, 2025 Open Source Hong Kong 開源香港 Python User Group Hong Kong (HKPUG) Hong Kong Creative Open Technology Association 香港創意開放科技協會 Read More COVID Policy Posted on September 26, 2023 September 20, 2024 Please refer to COVID website of the Hong Kong Government. Read More PyCon HK 2023: Get Your Early Bird Ticket Now! Posted on September 25, 2023 September 28, 2023 The annual Python conference, PyCon HK 2023 on 20231111 is heating up🔥, and Early Bird tickets are now available! Read More Get Ready for the Blind Bird Ticket of PyCon HK 2023! Posted on July 21, 2023 July 21, 2023 Mark your calendars! On August 8, 2023, at 8:00 PM, the Blind Bird Tickets for PyCon HK 2023 will go on sale! 🎉 Read More [Closed] PyCon HK 2023 – Call For Proposal Posted on July 18, 2023 July 18, 2023 The Call for Proposal (CFP) of PyCon Hong Kong 2023 is now closed! Read More PyCon HK 2023 – Call For Proposal Posted on April 19, 2023 June 29, 2023 he Call for Proposals for PyCon HK 2023 has now started! Read More Procedures for Reporting Incidents – As of 2023 Posted on April 1, 2023 July 19, 2025 If you believe someone is in physical danger, including from themselves, the most important thing is to get that person help. Please contact the appropriate crisis number, non-emergency number, or police number. If you are a PyCon HK attendee, you can consult with a volunteer or staff member to help find an appropriate number. If… Read More Enforcement Procedures – As of 2023 Posted on April 1, 2023 July 19, 2025 This document summarizes the procedures the PyCon US staff uses to enforce the Code of Conduct. Summary of processes When the work group receives a report of a possible Code of Conduct violation, it will: Acknowledge the report Reporters should receive an emailed acknowledgment of the receipt of their report within 24 hours. Conflict of… Read More Code of Conduct – As of 2023 Posted on April 1, 2023 July 19, 2025 PyCon Hong Kong is a community conference intended for networking and collaboration in the developer community. We value the participation of each member of the Python community and want all attendees to have an enjoyable and fulfilling experience. Accordingly, all attendees are expected to show respect and courtesy to other attendees throughout the conference and… Read More Previous 1 2 Instagram LinkedIn Facebook Twitter YouTube Search for: Archives Archives Select Month November 2024 October 2024 September 2024 July 2024 April 2024 December 2023 October 2023 September 2023 July 2023 April 2023 November 2022 October 2022 August 2022 October 2021 September 2021 May 2021 November 2020 October 2020 September 2020 May 2020 April 2020 November 2018 October 2018 September 2018 August 2018 November 2017 October 2016 November 2015 History 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020-fall 2020-spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 ©2026 PyCon HK | Powered by SuperbThemes! →"
