    "visibleText": "Automating Business Tasks with Langchain and Python - PyCon HK Skip to content Menu PyCon HK Conference Highlights Schedule 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 Sponsors 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 Communities 2024 2023 2022 Booths 2024 2023 Organizers 2024 2023 2022 Volunteers 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 PyCon HK Automating Business Tasks with Langchain and Python Posted on October 10, 2023 July 20, 2025 Time Slot: Track 1 14:40-15:10 Language: English Speaker: Dr. Chung Ng | PCCW-HKT | Hong Kong As modern businesses endeavor to improve efficiency and streamline operations, automation has taken center stage. This presentation will focus on how Langchain, in conjunction with Python, can automate complex tasks and foster significant process improvements. The presentation will unfold a four-level approach, explaining how Langchain can be utilized in different scenarios, with varying degrees of complexity and requirements: 1. Pre-set Knowledge with Langchain: In the first level, we’ll discuss how to leverage Langchain’s pre-set knowledge for automating routine tasks. We will delve into its default capabilities and demonstrate how these can be harnessed effectively to drive automation. 2. Incorporating New Topics and Styles: Level two will demonstrate how to enrich Langchain’s performance by integrating new topics and styles into its knowledge base. This addition broadens the range of tasks Langchain can handle, making it a versatile tool for diverse automation needs. 3. Complex Automation with Multiple Steps: Moving on to the third level, we’ll examine how Langchain can manage multi-step tasks that require advanced logic and sequence. We’ll showcase examples of such tasks and how Langchain’s capabilities can be extended to tackle them. 4. Output Formatting and Automation Plug-ins: Lastly, we will focus on Langchain’s output management features. We’ll discuss how to customize output formats and integrate automation plug-ins, enhancing both the versatility and usability of Langchain-powered solutions. This presentation aims to illustrate how the convergence of Langchain and Python can bring about significant automation benefits. Attendees will gain valuable insights into practical implementations of this methodology and how it can be leveraged to improve operational efficiency in their respective organizations. Dr. Chung Ng Dr. Chung is a SVP at Group CTO Office of the HKT/PCCW Group, where he’s responsible for leading the group’s product and technology roadmap and strategic development. He also represents the group as board members of Lynx Analytics and Bindo Labs. Before HKT/PCCW, Chung contributed to the Big Data/AI strategy at Telstra as well as its international growth strategy. Prior to Telstra, Chung was an Associate Partner of Cluster Technology Limited which serves the Greater China market with professional services and solutions in high-performance computing, machine learning, big data, and public cloud. In 2008, Chung joined McKinsey & Company in the Hong Kong office. He received his DPhil in Information Engineering from the University of Oxford and held the Croucher Foundation Scholarship to work toward his research degree in wireless ad-hoc networks. Chung also received BEng and MPhil in Information Engineering from the Chinese University of Hong Kong. Instagram LinkedIn Facebook Twitter YouTube Search for: Archives Archives Select Month November 2024 October 2024 September 2024 July 2024 April 2024 December 2023 October 2023 September 2023 July 2023 April 2023 November 2022 October 2022 August 2022 October 2021 September 2021 May 2021 November 2020 October 2020 September 2020 May 2020 April 2020 November 2018 October 2018 September 2018 August 2018 November 2017 October 2016 November 2015 History 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020-fall 2020-spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 ©2026 PyCon HK | Powered by SuperbThemes! ← [CANCELED] Building IoT Applications with Python and Embedded Systems ← Innovations and Cross-domain Applications of Python and Machine Learning in the Smart Logistics Field"
