    "visibleText": "Large Language Model Deployment and Fine-tuning with Python - PyCon HK Skip to content Menu PyCon HK Conference Highlights Schedule 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 Sponsors 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 Communities 2024 2023 2022 Booths 2024 2023 Organizers 2024 2023 2022 Volunteers 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 PyCon HK Large Language Model Deployment and Fine-tuning with Python Posted on October 10, 2023 October 18, 2023 Time Slot: Track 1 16:20-16:35 Language: English Speaker: Mr. Haowen Huang | AWS | Hong Kong The wave of Generative AI and large language models (LLMs) is sweeping the world, revolutionising various industries. This interesting talk will focus on how to efficiently and easily deploy and fine-tune various open-source large language models (LLMs) using Python. Mr. Haowen Huang Haowen Huang, a senior developer advocate at AWS based in Hong Kong, brings over 20 years of experience in cloud computing, internet, and telecommunications industries. His research focuses on Generative AI, Large Language Models (LLMs), machine learning, and data science. Instagram LinkedIn Facebook Twitter YouTube Search for: Archives Archives Select Month November 2024 October 2024 September 2024 July 2024 April 2024 December 2023 October 2023 September 2023 July 2023 April 2023 November 2022 October 2022 August 2022 October 2021 September 2021 May 2021 November 2020 October 2020 September 2020 May 2020 April 2020 November 2018 October 2018 September 2018 August 2018 November 2017 October 2016 November 2015 History 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020-fall 2020-spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 ©2026 PyCon HK | Powered by SuperbThemes! ← Automating Victory: Beating browser games with accessible Python ← As Soft as Ever Changing — Clean Architecture in Python"
