    "visibleText": "Security 101 for package maintainers - PyCon HK Skip to content Menu PyCon HK Conference Highlights Schedule 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 Sponsors 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 Communities 2024 2023 2022 Booths 2024 2023 Organizers 2024 2023 2022 Volunteers 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 PyCon HK Security 101 for package maintainers Posted on October 10, 2023 July 20, 2025 Time Slot: Track 1 16:40-16:55 Language: English Speaker: Ms. Cheuk Ting Ho (何卓婷) | Python Software Foundation | UK Are you a package maintainer? Whether you are a maintainer or not, there are security practices that can make you and the software that you work on safer for folks to use. In this short talk, we will go over some of these practices and you can check how many of them you are doing right now, and how many of them you are going to practice after this talk. Ms. Cheuk Ting Ho (何卓婷) Before working in Developer Relations, Cheuk has been a Data Scientist in various companies which demands high numerical and programmatical skills, especially in Python. To follow her passion for the tech community, Cheuk is now the Developer Advocate. Cheuk also contributes to multiple Open Source libraries like Hypothesis, Pandas and Django. Besides her work, Cheuk enjoys talking about Python on personal streaming platforms and podcasts. Cheuk has also been a speaker at Universities and various conferences. Besides speaking at conferences, Cheuk also organises events for developers. Conferences that Cheuk has organized include EuroPython (which she is a board member), PyData Global and Pyjamas Conf. Believing in Tech Diversity and Inclusion, Cheuk constantly organizes workshops and mentored sprints for minority groups. In 2021, Cheuk has become a Python Software Foundation fellow. Instagram LinkedIn Facebook Twitter YouTube Search for: Archives Archives Select Month November 2024 October 2024 September 2024 July 2024 April 2024 December 2023 October 2023 September 2023 July 2023 April 2023 November 2022 October 2022 August 2022 October 2021 September 2021 May 2021 November 2020 October 2020 September 2020 May 2020 April 2020 November 2018 October 2018 September 2018 August 2018 November 2017 October 2016 November 2015 History 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020-fall 2020-spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 ©2026 PyCon HK | Powered by SuperbThemes! ← Playing with PiPico ← Empowering Educators: Automated Assignment Scoring via Generative AI with Python"
