    "visibleText": "Simplifying Machine Learning pipeline using MySQL HeatWave - PyCon HK Skip to content Menu PyCon HK Conference Highlights Schedule 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 Sponsors 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 Communities 2024 2023 2022 Booths 2024 2023 Organizers 2024 2023 2022 Volunteers 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 PyCon HK Simplifying Machine Learning pipeline using MySQL HeatWave Posted on October 10, 2023 October 12, 2023 Time Slot: Track 1 17:00-17:30 Language: English Speaker: Mr. Ivan Ma | Oracle Systems Hong Kong Ltd | Hong Kong Machine Learning allows prediction, recommendation based on model which is built from dataset. Data preparation, sampling, algorithms selection, hyper parameter tuning can be complex in order to build a model. The session will cover the what MySQL HeatWave AutoML can help to simplify the complexity of ML pipeline. Data is really easy with database, what it is great if it is embedded with ML capability. Come and join us to share your experience and discuss. Mr. Ivan Ma Ivan Ma has over 20+ years with IT technologies around Databases, Infrastructure and projects development. He is leading the Hong Kong MySQL User Group. His career started as developer and as Consultant/Principal Solution Architect in Sybase for over 10 years. He joined Oracle from the Sun Microsystems acquisition and now he is working in MySQL Team as Master Principal Solutions Engineer. Instagram LinkedIn Facebook Twitter YouTube Search for: Archives Archives Select Month November 2024 October 2024 September 2024 July 2024 April 2024 December 2023 October 2023 September 2023 July 2023 April 2023 November 2022 October 2022 August 2022 October 2021 September 2021 May 2021 November 2020 October 2020 September 2020 May 2020 April 2020 November 2018 October 2018 September 2018 August 2018 November 2017 October 2016 November 2015 History 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020-fall 2020-spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 ©2026 PyCon HK | Powered by SuperbThemes! ← As Soft as Ever Changing — Clean Architecture in Python ← ZKML: turning your ML model into a ZK circuit"
